setup/nginx.conf<pre><code># Bottleneck: balanceamento de carga.
# O Nginx é o único serviço exposto (porta 8080 do host). Ele distribui as
# requisições entre as réplicas do gateway (round robin, o padrão do upstream).

user  nginx;
worker_processes  auto;

error_log  /var/log/nginx/error.log notice;
pid        /run/nginx.pid;

events {
    worker_connections  1024;
}

http {

    # DNS interno do Docker: com "resolve" (nginx &gt;= 1.27.3) o upstream é
    # re-resolvido a cada 10 s, então "docker compose up --scale gateway=N"
    # entra no balanceamento sem precisar de nginx -s reload
    resolver 127.0.0.11 valid=10s ipv6=off;

    upstream gateways {
        zone gateways 64k;
        server gateway:8080 resolve;
        # conexões reaproveitadas com o gateway (menos handshakes sob carga)
        keepalive 32;
    }

    log_format upstream '$remote_addr "$request" $status -&gt; $upstream_addr ($upstream_response_time s)';
    access_log /var/log/nginx/access.log upstream;

    server {
        listen 80;
        server_tokens off;

        # métricas e detalhes do actuator ficam só na rede interna
        # (o Prometheus fala direto com o gateway); o health fica público
        location = /gateway/actuator/health {
            proxy_pass http://gateways;
        }
        location /gateway/actuator {
            return 404;
        }

        location / {
            proxy_pass         http://gateways;
            proxy_http_version 1.1;
            proxy_set_header   Connection        "";
            proxy_set_header   Host              $host;
            proxy_set_header   X-Real-IP         $remote_addr;
            proxy_set_header   X-Forwarded-For   $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
            proxy_set_header   X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        }
    }
}
</code></pre> <p>What goes beyond the course's hands-on 7:</p> Directive Why <code>resolver 127.0.0.11</code> + <code>server gateway:8080 resolve</code> Nginx re-resolves Docker's DNS every 10 s. With <code>docker compose up --scale gateway=N</code> the new replicas join the balancing without <code>nginx -s reload</code> (in the hands-on, Nginx only resolves at startup). <code>server gateway.store.svc.cluster.local:8080 resolve</code> + <code>resolver kube-dns...</code> (only in <code>k8s/lb.yaml</code>) On EKS, Nginx starts before the gateway (<code>infra</code> applies <code>lb</code> and each service deploys itself afterwards). Without <code>resolve</code>, Nginx crashes with host not found and <code>infra</code> fails waiting for <code>lb</code>, as happened on 16/11. With it, <code>lb</code> becomes ready, responds <code>502</code> until the <code>gateway</code> Service exists and then starts forwarding on its own. Nginx's resolver does not use the k8s search domains, hence the fully qualified name. <code>keepalive 32</code> + <code>proxy_http_version 1.1</code> Reuses connections to the gateway: fewer TCP handshakes under load. <code>keepalive_time 10s</code> (only in <code>k8s/lb.yaml</code>) In k8s, Nginx talks to the <code>gateway</code> Service, which balances connections, not requests: an open connection stays on the same pod. By closing each connection after 10 s, the replicas created by the HPA join the split in ≈ 35–40 s instead of ≈ 1.5 min (finding from the HPA test). Not needed on compose: there Nginx sees each replica through DNS and splits the requests itself. <code>location /gateway/actuator { return 404; }</code> Actuator metrics stay on the internal network only (Prometheus talks directly to the gateway). <code>log_format upstream</code> The access log shows which replica (<code>$upstream_addr</code>) served each request.

k8s/lb.yaml<pre><code># Bottleneck: balanceamento de carga no EKS.
#
#   internet -&gt; ELB da AWS (Service type LoadBalancer)
#            -&gt; pods do Nginx (lb, 2 réplicas)
#            -&gt; Service gateway (ClusterIP) -&gt; pods do gateway (2+ réplicas)
#
# O Nginx é a única porta de entrada: gateway, auth, account e exchange são
# ClusterIP (camada confiável), como no compose.
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: lb-configmap
data:
  nginx.conf: |
    worker_processes auto;
    pid /tmp/nginx.pid;
    error_log /dev/stderr notice;

    events {
        worker_connections 1024;
    }

    http {
        client_body_temp_path /tmp/client_temp;
        proxy_temp_path       /tmp/proxy_temp;
        fastcgi_temp_path     /tmp/fastcgi_temp;
        uwsgi_temp_path       /tmp/uwsgi_temp;
        scgi_temp_path        /tmp/scgi_temp;

        log_format upstream '$remote_addr "$request" $status -&gt; $upstream_addr ($upstream_response_time s)';
        access_log /dev/stdout upstream;

        # "resolve": o nome é resolvido em tempo de execução, então o Nginx sobe
        # mesmo antes de o Service gateway existir (responde 502 até ele
        # aparecer) em vez de cair com "host not found" e travar o infra.
        # O resolver do Nginx não usa os domínios de busca: nome completo,
        # com o namespace (store).
        resolver kube-dns.kube-system.svc.cluster.local valid=10s ipv6=off;

        # no k8s o Service "gateway" já é um IP virtual que distribui entre
        # os pods; o Nginx mantém conexões abertas com ele (keepalive)
        upstream gateways {
            zone gateways 64k;
            server gateway.store.svc.cluster.local:8080 resolve;
            keepalive 32;
            # o Service balanceia conexões, não requisições: sem limite, cada
            # conexão fica no mesmo pod por 1000 requisições e as réplicas que o
            # HPA cria levam ~1,5 min para receber carga (~35-40 s com 10 s)
            keepalive_time 10s;
        }

        server {
            listen 8080;
            server_tokens off;

            location = /lb/health {
                access_log off;
                return 200 "ok\n";
            }

            location = /gateway/actuator/health {
                proxy_pass http://gateways;
            }
            location /gateway/actuator {
                return 404;
            }

            location / {
                proxy_pass         http://gateways;
                proxy_http_version 1.1;
                proxy_set_header   Connection        "";
                proxy_set_header   Host              $host;
                proxy_set_header   X-Real-IP         $remote_addr;
                proxy_set_header   X-Forwarded-For   $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
                proxy_set_header   X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
            }
        }
    }
---
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: lb
  labels:
    app: lb
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: lb
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: lb
    spec:
      securityContext:
        runAsNonRoot: true
        runAsUser: 101
        runAsGroup: 101
        seccompProfile:
          type: RuntimeDefault
      containers:
        - name: nginx
          image: nginx:1.29-alpine
          ports:
            - containerPort: 8080
          readinessProbe:
            httpGet:
              path: /lb/health
              port: 8080
            periodSeconds: 5
          resources:
            requests:
              memory: "32Mi"
              cpu: "50m"
            limits:
              memory: "128Mi"
              cpu: "500m"
          securityContext:
            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
            capabilities:
              drop: [ "ALL" ]
          volumeMounts:
            - name: config
              mountPath: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
              subPath: nginx.conf
              readOnly: true
            - name: tmp
              mountPath: /tmp
      volumes:
        - name: config
          configMap:
            name: lb-configmap
        - name: tmp
          emptyDir: {}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: lb
spec:
  type: LoadBalancer
  selector:
    app: lb
  ports:
    - name: http
      protocol: TCP
      port: 80
      targetPort: 8080
</code></pre>

load/store.jsscripts/load-test.shscripts/load-matrix.shscripts/kind-up.shscripts/hpa-record.pyscripts/eks-hpa.shscripts/fill-eks-hpa.py <pre><code>// Teste de carga da plataforma (k6). Rodar com ./scripts/load-test.sh.
//
// Variáveis:
//   BASE_URL  http://lb (dentro da rede do compose) ou o endereço do ELB
//   SCENARIO  auth | exchange | login | mixed           (padrão: mixed)
//   PROFILE   smoke | load | stress | spike              (padrão: load)
//   VUS       usuários virtuais no platô                 (padrão: 50)
//   DURATION  duração do platô                           (padrão: 1m)
//   USERS     contas criadas no setup e reutilizadas     (padrão: 20)
//   NAME      nome do resultado em load/results/          (padrão: SCENARIO-PROFILE)
//   THINK     pausa entre ações, em s (padrão: 0.5-1.5 aleatório; 0 = sem pausa,
//             para achar o limite de vazão)
//
// Cenários:
//   auth      GET /auth/me + GET /accounts/{id}: rota protegida -&gt; gateway valida o
//             token (Redis ou Auth) -&gt; serviço. Mede cache do token e balanceamento.
//   exchange  GET /exchange/USD/BRL (e EUR/BRL): mede o cache da cotação.
//   login     POST /auth/login: caminho caro (hash da senha + emissão do JWT).
//   mixed     80% leitura autenticada, 15% câmbio, 5% login (uso "real" da loja).

import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';
import exec from 'k6/execution';
import { textSummary } from 'https://jslib.k6.io/k6-summary/0.1.0/index.js';

const BASE_URL = __ENV.BASE_URL || 'http://lb';
const SCENARIO = __ENV.SCENARIO || 'mixed';
const PROFILE = __ENV.PROFILE || 'load';
const VUS = parseInt(__ENV.VUS || '50', 10);
const DURATION = __ENV.DURATION || '1m';
const USERS = parseInt(__ENV.USERS || '20', 10);
const NAME = __ENV.NAME || `${SCENARIO}-${PROFILE}`;
const THINK = __ENV.THINK;
const PASSWORD = 'carga-senha-123';

const PROFILES = {
  // 1 usuário, só para ver se o script e a plataforma funcionam
  smoke: [
    { duration: '1s', target: 1 },
    { duration: '20s', target: 1 },
  ],
  // carga esperada: sobe, mantém o platô, desce
  load: [
    { duration: '20s', target: VUS },
    { duration: DURATION, target: VUS },
    { duration: '10s', target: 0 },
  ],
  // aumenta até achar o ponto de quebra (onde p95 ou erros estouram)
  stress: [
    { duration: '30s', target: VUS },
    { duration: '30s', target: VUS * 2 },
    { duration: '30s', target: VUS * 4 },
    { duration: '30s', target: VUS * 8 },
    { duration: '20s', target: 0 },
  ],
  // pico repentino (ex.: promoção): a plataforma se recupera?
  spike: [
    { duration: '10s', target: Math.max(1, Math.floor(VUS / 10)) },
    { duration: '5s', target: VUS * 4 },
    { duration: '30s', target: VUS * 4 },
    { duration: '5s', target: Math.max(1, Math.floor(VUS / 10)) },
    { duration: '30s', target: Math.max(1, Math.floor(VUS / 10)) },
    { duration: '5s', target: 0 },
  ],
};

export const options = {
  scenarios: {
    [SCENARIO]: {
      executor: 'ramping-vus',
      startVUs: 0,
      stages: PROFILES[PROFILE] || PROFILES.load,
      gracefulRampDown: '10s',
    },
  },
  // SLO do projeto (ver docs/devops/custos-sla.md): o k6 sai com código 99 se estourar.
  // Só conta a fase de teste (phase:test): o cadastro/login do setup() fica de fora.
  thresholds: {
    'http_req_failed{phase:test}': ['rate&lt;0.01'],
    'http_req_duration{phase:test,expected_response:true}': ['p(95)&lt;500', 'p(99)&lt;1500'],
    'http_reqs{phase:test}': ['count&gt;0'],
    checks: ['rate&gt;0.99'],
  },
  summaryTrendStats: ['avg', 'med', 'p(90)', 'p(95)', 'p(99)', 'max'],
  setupTimeout: '2m',
  tags: { testid: NAME },
};

const JSON_HEADERS = { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' };

// tag "phase": separa o setup() (cadastro/login das contas) da carga medida
const tags = (name, phase = 'test') =&gt; ({ name, phase });

function login(email, phase = 'test') {
  const res = http.post(`${BASE_URL}/auth/login`, JSON.stringify({ email, password: PASSWORD }), {
    headers: JSON_HEADERS,
    tags: tags('POST /auth/login', phase),
  });
  const cookie = res.cookies.__store_jwt_token;
  return cookie &amp;&amp; cookie.length ? cookie[0].value : null;
}

// Cria USERS contas e faz login uma vez: os VUs reutilizam os tokens, como
// usuários reais navegando logados (é isso que o cache do token aproveita).
export function setup() {
  const run = `${Date.now()}`;
  const users = [];
  for (let i = 0; i &lt; USERS; i++) {
    const email = `carga+${run}-${i}@store.test`;
    const reg = http.post(
      `${BASE_URL}/auth/register`,
      JSON.stringify({ name: `Carga ${i}`, email, password: PASSWORD }),
      { headers: JSON_HEADERS, tags: tags('setup', 'setup') },
    );
    if (reg.status !== 200 &amp;&amp; reg.status !== 201) {
      exec.test.abort(`POST /auth/register respondeu ${reg.status}: ${reg.body}`);
    }
    const token = login(email, 'setup');
    if (!token) exec.test.abort('login não devolveu o cookie __store_jwt_token');
    const me = http.get(`${BASE_URL}/auth/me`, {
      headers: { Cookie: `__store_jwt_token=${token}` },
      tags: tags('setup', 'setup'),
    });
    users.push({ email, token, id: me.json('id') });
  }
  return { users };
}

function authRead(user) {
  const params = { headers: { Cookie: `__store_jwt_token=${user.token}` } };
  const me = http.get(`${BASE_URL}/auth/me`, Object.assign({ tags: tags('GET /auth/me') }, params));
  check(me, { 'auth/me 200': (r) =&gt; r.status === 200 });
  const acc = http.get(`${BASE_URL}/accounts/${user.id}`, Object.assign({ tags: tags('GET /accounts/{id}') }, params));
  check(acc, { 'accounts/{id} 200': (r) =&gt; r.status === 200 });
}

function exchange(user) {
  const pair = Math.random() &lt; 0.8 ? 'USD/BRL' : 'EUR/BRL';
  const res = http.get(`${BASE_URL}/exchange/${pair}`, {
    headers: { Cookie: `__store_jwt_token=${user.token}` },
    tags: tags('GET /exchange/{from}/{to}'),
  });
  check(res, {
    'exchange 200': (r) =&gt; r.status === 200,
    'exchange sell &gt;= buy': (r) =&gt; r.status === 200 &amp;&amp; r.json('sell') &gt;= r.json('buy'),
  });
}

function doLogin(user) {
  check(login(user.email), { 'login devolve token': (t) =&gt; !!t });
}

export default function (data) {
  const user = data.users[(exec.vu.idInTest - 1) % data.users.length];
  switch (SCENARIO) {
    case 'auth':
      authRead(user);
      break;
    case 'exchange':
      exchange(user);
      break;
    case 'login':
      doLogin(user);
      break;
    default: {
      const r = Math.random();
      if (r &lt; 0.8) authRead(user);
      else if (r &lt; 0.95) exchange(user);
      else doLogin(user);
    }
  }
  // "tempo de leitura" do usuário: sem isso cada VU vira um loop sem pausa
  if (THINK === undefined) sleep(0.5 + Math.random());
  else if (parseFloat(THINK) &gt; 0) sleep(parseFloat(THINK));
}

// Resumo no terminal + JSON completo + uma linha de tabela markdown, para o
// scripts/load-matrix.sh juntar os resultados em load/results/RESULTS.md.
export function handleSummary(data) {
  const m = data.metrics;
  // só a fase de teste (submétricas criadas pelos thresholds com {phase:test})
  const d = m['http_req_duration{phase:test,expected_response:true}'];
  const reqs = m['http_reqs{phase:test}'];
  const failed = m['http_req_failed{phase:test}'];
  const fmt = (v) =&gt; (v === undefined ? '-' : v.toFixed(0));
  const row =
    `| ${NAME} | ${SCENARIO} | ${PROFILE} | ${m.vus_max ? m.vus_max.values.max : '-'} ` +
    `| ${reqs.values.count} | ${reqs.values.rate.toFixed(1)} ` +
    `| ${fmt(d.values.med)} | ${fmt(d.values['p(95)'])} | ${fmt(d.values['p(99)'])} ` +
    `| ${(failed.values.rate * 100).toFixed(2)} % |\n`;
  return {
    stdout: textSummary(data, { indent: ' ', enableColors: true }),
    [`/results/${NAME}.json`]: JSON.stringify(data, null, 2),
    [`/results/${NAME}.row.md`]: row,
  };
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Roda um teste de carga (k6, via Docker) contra a plataforma.
#
#   ./scripts/load-test.sh                               # cenário mixed, perfil load, 50 VUs
#   SCENARIO=auth PROFILE=stress VUS=50 ./scripts/load-test.sh
#   BASE_URL=http://&lt;elb-da-aws&gt; ./scripts/load-test.sh  # contra o EKS
#   BASE_URL=http://&lt;elb&gt; PROMETHEUS_RW_URL=http://host.docker.internal:9090 ./scripts/load-test.sh
#                                                        # EKS + métricas no Prometheus do cluster
#
# Sem BASE_URL, o k6 entra na rede do compose e chama o lb por dentro (http://lb),
# e manda as métricas para o Prometheus do compose (aparecem no Grafana, linha
